# This file contains example REST API requests for testing the queue management system.

### Root (welcome)
GET http://localhost:3000/
###

### Hello (simple greeting)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/hello
###

### Team members (all)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/team
###

### Departments (unique list)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/departments
###

### Get caller by account number
GET http://localhost:3000/api/callers/ACCT12345
###

### Add a new call to the queue
POST http://localhost:3000/api/queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"accountNumber": "ACCT-1234",
	"department": "Support",
	"issue": "I had a question about my recent billing statement."
}
###

### Get full queue (all statuses)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/queue
###

### Get queue filtered by status (comma-separated)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/queue?status=waiting,completed
###

### Get the next waiting caller (global)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/queue/next
###

### Get the next waiting caller for a department
GET http://localhost:3000/api/queue/next?department=support
###

### Verify a queued call (mark in-progress) - verified = true
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/queue/1/verify?verified=true
###

### Verify a queued call (reject) - verified = false
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/queue/1/verify?verified=false
###

### Mark an in-progress call as completed
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/queue/1/complete
###
